Bitcoin Trend Detection Trading System - Project Notes

Started with a boring school assignment - BYOP. Everyone's doing student performance predictors.

Then realized - I have 7.5M rows of Bitcoin 1-minute OHLC data. That's actually useful.

Initial thought: can I predict next minute direction? Scalp like I do in options.
Nope. 1-minute crypto data is too noisy. Spreads and fees would kill any micro edge.

ChatGPT was right - scalping won't work here. Switched to trend detection instead.

So instead of "will price go up next minute", the real question is "is a real trend starting right now?"

This led to thinking about labels. Labels are everything. Model only learns what labels teach it.

Started simple: just label if price goes up or down. Too noisy.

Better: define profitability. What if I encoded risk management INTO the labels?

Triple barrier idea came up. TP and SL thresholds. Look 30 minutes ahead.

But wait - I don't want to be symmetric about this. I want the system to be cautious.
TP = +1.5% (hard to trigger BUY, means strong move)
SL = -0.7% (easy to trigger SELL, quick to detect danger)

Why? Because avoiding bad trades > chasing every possible trade.

This naturally creates imbalance: more SELL labels than BUY. That's the point. It's intentional bias toward caution.

For the model output - initially thought softmax. But softmax forces a choice even when both signals are weak.

Sigmoid is better. Two independent outputs. Can say "both signals weak, don't trade". That's realistic.

Final label logic is clean:
- Look ahead 30 minutes
- Price hits +1.5% first? BUY
- Price hits -0.7% first? SELL
- Neither? Do nothing (no trade)

One thing ChatGPT kept hammering: don't expect 90% accuracy. Markets are random. 50-65% is actually good.

Real edge isn't accuracy. It's feature quality + uncertainty filtering. Trade less, trade better.

So the pipeline is:
1. Get labels (done, or will be this week)
2. Engineer features (what patterns show a trend is starting?)
3. Train model with sigmoid outputs
4. Build decision logic with thresholds
5. Backtest to see if it actually makes money
6. Then we know if it's real

Key things to NOT forget:
- No using future data in features (easy to accidentally leak)
- Time-based split, never shuffle
- Class weights during training (because imbalance is intentional)
- Test on 200k rows first, not all 7.5M (memory)
- The uncertainty filter matters as much as the predictions

implemented full labelling code. Realized later having a third signal where the model just refuses to trade would also be good.
Not hittign either stop loss or take profit within max horizon would trigger refusal signal marked as "idk_label" for weak trend and low deviation signal

Ran programme labelling.py and noticed: overalapping between the three signals is 0 so code logic is sound, no trade ratio is 0.9322 or 93.22%. meaning the resultimg machine learning model will play it very cautious, just as we intended.
